  <page_number>94</page_number>
  <running_head>Varia Poemata</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Pulchrú</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">AD PETRUM POPPÆUM</l>
    <l n="2" type="heading" level="2">Poetam.</l>
    <l n="3" para="true">
      <i>LASCIVA Musæ cantica virgines</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Odere, blandas delicias Lyræ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5">
      <i>Arcent profanæ, non Poetam</i>
    </l>
    <l n="6">
      <i>Pierij patiuntur antri</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>Sacris adesse, &amp; tollere Delphicas</i>
    </l>
    <l n="8">
      <i>Æterna Lauros præmia, si probat</i>
    </l>
    <l n="9">
      <i>Obscœnus incestos amores,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="10">
      <i>Furta docens Veneris nefandæ.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="11">
      <i>Sunt hæc canora murmura tibiæ,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="12">
      <i>Poppæ, Musis dulcia, Numinis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>Quæ facta supremi recensent,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="14">
      <i>Utque suum moderatur orbem,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="15">
      <i>Seu savientes[?] sacrilega manu</i>
    </l>
    <l n="16">
      <i>Cogat Gigantes regna Proserpinæ</i>
    </l>
    <l n="17">
      <i>Umbrasque pallentes adire,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="18">
      <i>Fulminea metuendus arce:</i>
    </l>
    <l n="19">
      <i>Seu copioso munere largior</i>
    </l>
    <l n="20">
      <i>Fœcundat agros, latáque pascuis</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>Armenta nutrit, pacibúsque</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>Agricolas recreat quietis.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>Sunt digna Phœbo, sunt Charitum choris</i>
    </l>
    <l n="24">
      <i>Jucunda, vates carmina quæ pius</i>
    </l>
    <l n="25">
      <i>Castúsque Musarum sacerdos</i>
    </l>
    <l n="26">
      <i>Virginibus puerisque cantat:</i>
    </l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The title line is set in capitals with a second line "Poetam." in small capitals; both are one heading. The verse lines are run together in one paragraph because no stanza breaks are visible. The word after "savientes" is uncertain: the scan shows an ligatured "sa" letter, possibly æ. Initial "L" of LASCIVA is a large letter joined to the word. Pierij's final letter is unclear.</notes>
</page>
